<title>SINGAPORE: Singapore March retail sales rise 1.5 pct on yr.</title>
<headline>Singapore March retail sales rise 1.5 pct on yr.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-05-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Singapore's retail sales index (base 1991) rose 1.5 percent in March compared to a year ago, a government official said on Monday.  </p>
<p>The official, quoting a report by the Statistics Office, said the index was up 12.7 percent compared with February.</p>
<p>Excluding motor vehicles, the index registered a month-on-month gain of 0.9 percent in March.</p>
<p>Total March retail sales were estimated at Singapore $2.00 billion.</p>
<p>The report said that year-on-year, in constant prices, the retail index rose by 3.2 percent.  </p>
<p>					 Month-on-month     Yr-on-yr</p>
<p>    Total index			   12.7		 1.5</p>
<p>    X-vehicle sales			0.9		 5.0</p>
<p>    Textiles/apparels		   -7.8		 1.0</p>
<p>    Furniture/household equipment   12.8		18.1</p>
<p>    Motor vehicles		     101.3	     -10.1</p>
<p>    Petrol stations		     -9.2		-7.1</p>
<p>    Department stores/supermarkets  -5.8		 4.1</p>
<p>    General provisions		  -7.5		 4.2</p>
<p>    Other retail			  18.2		 6.1</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65 8703199)</p>
